{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"d9e5e9762f5a2f82f7df5024749673c9c7a801081d50ecde2625282e86eed214","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_99e1b16340409ed7659093f4d2280ced440f614fa80bbcdda48f142004b11f83","overall_assessment":"The paper is generally well-organized and clearly written, with a logical flow from motivation to model architecture, training, and experiments. The notation is consistent and well-defined, and the algorithmic presentation is clear. The main clarity weakness is a minor inconsistency in the mathematical notation for the memory extraction in Section 3.1, where the backward RNN symbol is used twice instead of the forward symbol. The figures and tables are well-captioned and provide useful textual descriptions of the results.","paper_id":"BJlxmAKlg","paper_identity_sha256":"af5938fb023d8c64e681eeb689cc0ccaf59b0af6d192b6a69ef1118958804ed3","prompt_identity_sha256":"b9f8b991349b937099a09c9f12489a316d4da3e73e3a1dbfbde2b06763082770","raw_response_sha256":"2ea9d1fe6ef8261d0806c88e311519d5d81b011d8b13606bfe868e103884e092","request_identity_sha256":"b26fabbf92b78c1940fa21a5cc6b02f98e66924fe9d690fc108aa1014dbf9e3a","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"552a1533b7b46bb28d3a21566cc19f292de0ba2013c378e28027325f27708855","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037","SRC-038","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured and clearly written. The introduction effectively motivates the problem and the proposed solution. The related work section is concise and well-organized. The model architecture is described in a logical order, and the training details are provided in a separate section. The experiments section is well-organized, with clear subsections for different datasets. The conclusion summarizes the main contributions and future work. The writing is generally clear and concise, with a good balance of technical detail and accessibility. The terminology is used consistently throughout the paper. The algorithm presentation is clear and easy to follow.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-013","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-030"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is generally consistent and well-defined. The key variables and parameters are clearly introduced and used consistently throughout the paper. The equations are well-formatted and easy to read. The derivations are clear and well-explained. However, there is a minor inconsistency in the notation for the memory extraction in Section 3.1. The paper states that the memory is extracted by mapping each symbolic in the passage to a contextual representation given by the concatenation of forward and backward RNN hidden states, i.e., m_k = [overleftarrow{p_n}^k, overleftarrow{p_n}^{|p_n| - k + 1}]. The first term should be the forward RNN hidden state, not the backward RNN hidden state. This is a minor issue, but it could be confusing for the reader. The notation for the attention score, the internal state, the termination gate, and the answer module is clear and consistent. The notation for the reward and the baseline is also clear and consistent.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-012","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036"],"review_text":"The figures and tables are well-captioned and provide useful textual descriptions of the results. Figure 1 shows the architecture of the ReasoNet, and the caption is clear and informative. Figure 2 shows a test example from the CNN dataset, and the caption provides a detailed description of the attention scores and the termination probability. The table in Figure 2 is readable and provides the necessary information. Figure 3 and Figure 4 show test examples from the Graph Reachability dataset, and the captions are clear and informative. The tables in Figure 3 and Figure 4 are readable and provide the necessary information. Table 1 shows the performance of the ReasoNet on the CNN and Daily Mail datasets, and the table is readable and provides the necessary information. Table 2 shows the reachability statistics of the Graph Reachability dataset, and the table is readable and provides the necessary information. Table 3 shows examples of a small graph and a large graph in the Graph Reachability dataset, and the table is readable and provides the necessary information. Table 4 shows the performance of the ReasoNet on the Graph Reachability dataset, and the table is readable and provides the necessary information.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"ecda52033a8576350dea70a08562e84852cfd43fc98014197ddebbd100a359b4","paper_id":"BJlxmAKlg","paper_ordinal":36,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"2ea9d1fe6ef8261d0806c88e311519d5d81b011d8b13606bfe868e103884e092","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJlxmAKlg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"1e5b223b7172dec81755432d6612d3c3a9e4a556830ffec9e9f2c5701041bf6b","request_identity_sha256":"b26fabbf92b78c1940fa21a5cc6b02f98e66924fe9d690fc108aa1014dbf9e3a","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1385,"prompt_tokens":19655,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":21040},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"b26fabbf92